1
00:00:00,496 --> 00:00:03,036
Teams glue together dozens of SaaS APIs.

2
00:00:03,056 --> 00:00:05,916
When one of them changes, or a token expires,

3
00:00:05,936 --> 00:00:07,772
someone finds out days later.

4
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:09,557
Meet H.A.D.E.S.

5
00:00:09,577 --> 00:00:11,956
Describe an integration in plain English.

6
00:00:11,976 --> 00:00:14,179
The AI builds it, a human approves it,

7
00:00:14,199 --> 00:00:16,226
and the platform runs it, heals it,

8
00:00:16,246 --> 00:00:18,976
and lets you manage it from Slack and WhatsApp.

9
00:00:20,721 --> 00:00:24,164
The dashboard shows what's live, what needs a decision,

10
00:00:24,184 --> 00:00:25,360
and overall health.

11
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:30,397
One rule runs everything: AI plans, deterministic code executes, humans approve.

12
00:00:31,707 --> 00:00:34,855
In AI Studio, I load a task-management API spec,

13
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,967
and describe the outcome I want.

14
00:00:39,524 --> 00:00:42,620
The AI extracts the services, operations and trigger.

15
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:46,440
Before generating, it shows exactly which records it will create.

16
00:00:46,662 --> 00:00:47,802
The pipeline runs.

17
00:00:47,822 --> 00:00:52,377
API discovery, a declarative config instead of code, schema validation,

18
00:00:52,397 --> 00:00:55,856
a security review, and safe tests on mocked responses.

19
00:00:55,876 --> 00:00:58,498
Six of six pass, and it goes to approval.

20
00:00:58,976 --> 00:01:02,512
Credentials go through a secure form into an encrypted vault.

21
00:01:02,532 --> 00:01:03,852
The AI never sees them.

22
00:01:07,432 --> 00:01:12,382
The admin sees every check: domain, schema, secrets, credential, tests,

23
00:01:12,402 --> 00:01:13,922
and an unchanged hash.

24
00:01:13,942 --> 00:01:16,512
Approval publishes exactly that hash.

25
00:01:16,532 --> 00:01:19,172
The AI can never approve its own work.

26
00:01:20,709 --> 00:01:22,945
The request also drafted a workflow:

27
00:01:22,965 --> 00:01:25,388
a graph of steps that can run manually,

28
00:01:25,408 --> 00:01:27,581
on a signed webhook, on a schedule,

29
00:01:27,601 --> 00:01:31,153
or automatically on a failure, an alert, or a new record.

30
00:01:32,869 --> 00:01:36,329
A dry run renders every request without sending anything.

31
00:01:38,384 --> 00:01:42,983
Data sources pull from Okta, CloudTrail, Google, Microsoft, GitHub,

32
00:01:43,003 --> 00:01:45,603
Jira and more, into one common format,

33
00:01:45,623 --> 00:01:48,636
with de-duplication and a dead-letter queue.

34
00:01:50,196 --> 00:01:51,246
Now, self-healing.

35
00:01:51,266 --> 00:01:53,030
I set it to fix automatically,

36
00:01:53,050 --> 00:01:55,528
then simulate the vendor changing its API.

37
00:01:55,753 --> 00:01:57,969
The next call fails with response drift.

38
00:01:57,989 --> 00:02:00,485
A field the integration depends on has moved.

39
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:07,725
H.A.D.E.S opens a case, collects evidence, finds the root cause,

40
00:02:07,745 --> 00:02:11,772
remaps the field, and publishes version one point zero point one,

41
00:02:11,792 --> 00:02:13,453
after validation and tests.

42
00:02:13,473 --> 00:02:14,761
Every step is logged.

43
00:02:14,781 --> 00:02:17,252
Critical fixes always wait for an admin.

44
00:02:22,090 --> 00:02:26,011
Monitoring tracks success rate, latency and error classes,

45
00:02:26,031 --> 00:02:28,118
with every repair in one place.

46
00:02:30,228 --> 00:02:32,692
From Slack, reply under a failure alert,

47
00:02:32,712 --> 00:02:35,920
and the AI investigates and explains the root cause.

48
00:02:36,395 --> 00:02:37,826
Ask it to fix the problem,

49
00:02:37,846 --> 00:02:40,448
and H.A.D.E.S posts Approve and Reject buttons.

50
00:02:40,468 --> 00:02:42,567
Only the person who asked can approve.

51
00:02:43,041 --> 00:02:47,053
On WhatsApp, admins get personal alerts with one-tap fix links,

52
00:02:47,073 --> 00:02:48,013
plus a chatbot.

53
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:52,642
In the app, the assistant answers from live data,

54
00:02:52,662 --> 00:02:55,649
and every change it proposes becomes an approval card.

55
00:02:57,216 --> 00:03:01,818
Bring any model: Bedrock, Gemini, OpenAI, Anthropic, Groq, Ollama,

56
00:03:01,838 --> 00:03:04,830
routed per task with budgets and fallbacks.

57
00:03:04,850 --> 00:03:08,332
A built-in offline model powered this entire demo.

58
00:03:09,776 --> 00:03:13,165
The tool registry sets which roles may run each tool,

59
00:03:13,185 --> 00:03:16,380
and which tools are exposed to AI agents over MCP.

60
00:03:16,604 --> 00:03:19,729
Versions are immutable, with one-click rollback,

61
00:03:19,749 --> 00:03:23,528
and the audit log records every action, by people, the AI,

62
00:03:23,548 --> 00:03:24,576
agents and chat.

63
00:03:26,016 --> 00:03:26,635
H.A.D.E.S.

64
00:03:26,655 --> 00:03:29,193
AI plans, code executes, humans approve.

65
00:03:29,213 --> 00:03:33,477
Live on Zoho Catalyst, with a hundred and ninety-two passing tests.

66
00:03:33,497 --> 00:03:34,756
Thanks for watching.

